# ICU (Intensive Care) Patient Flow

## 0. Overview

This file is the direct ICU flow source of truth for the HOSSPI HMS implementation plan. ICU is a **clinical overlay on the IPD encounter** — not a parallel admission system. It should stay aligned with the backend IPD flow ICU actions (`include_icu`, `icu_queue_scope`, `start-icu-stay`, `end-icu-stay`, observations, critical alerts), the Flutter ICU workspace, and the upstream/downstream flows in [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](./ipd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](./opd-flow.mdc), and [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc).

## 1. Goal

Enable ICU nurses, intensivists, bed managers, and escalation coordinators to run critical-care work end-to-end: receive escalated inpatients, manage ICU stays and ICU beds, record high-acuity observations and vitals, raise and resolve critical alerts, perform ICU rounds, place inpatient orders, coordinate step-down transfers, and signal discharge readiness — all anchored to the **same IPD admission / encounter**.

Emergency `ICU` disposition and OPD `ADMITTED` handoff must land in the ICU workspace with source context preserved. Deliver a **professional, calm, critical-care workspace** optimized for rapid triage: role-focused queues, critical-alert prominence, predictable primary actions, patient context at a glance, and no raw internal identifiers in the UI.

### Central encounter rule

Every ICU stay, observation, alert, round, order, and transfer attaches to the **IPD admission / encounter**. ICU does not create duplicate admission records. OPD owns outpatient completion; IPD owns admission lifecycle; ICU owns intensive-care overlay while the patient is in critical care.

---

## 2. Position in the Patient Journey

ICU sits **after** OPD/Emergency admission intake and **on top of** the IPD encounter.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    OPD[OPD disposition ADMITTED] --> IPD[IPD encounter created]
    EMR[Emergency stabilize → ICU disposition] --> IPD
    REF[Referral / planned admission] --> IPD
    IPD --> BED[Bed allocation — ICU ward]
    BED --> ICU_START[start-icu-stay]
    ICU_START --> ICU_WS[ICU workspace]
    ICU_WS --> CARE[Monitoring, orders, rounds, alerts]
    CARE --> STEP[Step-down transfer / end ICU stay]
    STEP --> IPD_WARD[IPD ward care continues]
    IPD_WARD --> DISCH[IPD discharge clearance]
```

| Upstream | Flow reference | ICU responsibility |
| -------- | -------------- | ------------------ |
| OPD doctor admits | [opd-flow §7](./opd-flow.mdc), stage `ADMITTED` | Show linked OPD encounter on ICU detail; do not recreate admission |
| Emergency ICU path | [ipd-flow §2.1](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Patients from emergency ICU flow appear on active ICU board |
| IPD bed manager | [ipd-flow §3, §14](./ipd-flow.mdc) | ICU bed board is ICU-ward scoped view of same bed catalog |
| IPD transfer | [ipd-flow §9](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Ward→ICU: complete transfer then `start-icu-stay`; step-down ends stay |
| Nursing | [app-write-up](../app-write-up.mdc) Nursing row | Shared vitals/MAR visibility; ICU owns stay-scoped observations/alerts |
| Theater post-op | [app-write-up](../app-write-up.mdc) Theater row | Post-op handoff summary on ICU detail when theatre reference exists |
| Billing | [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Orders use `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel`; clearance stays in Billing/IPD |
| Discharge | [ipd-flow §10–§12](./ipd-flow.mdc) | ICU marks readiness only; IPD/Discharge own multi-step clearance |

---

## 3. Step-by-Step ICU Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | ICU eligibility identified | Patient needs critical care from ward escalation, emergency disposition, OPD admission to ICU, theater post-op, or planned ICU admission. | Doctor / Emergency clinician / Bed manager |
| 2 | ICU bed allocation | Suitable ICU/NICU bed is reserved or assigned via IPD bed management. | Bed manager / ICU charge nurse |
| 3 | ICU stay opened | `start-icu-stay` opens an active ICU stay on the IPD admission. | Intensivist / ICU nurse / Authorized clinician |
| 4 | ICU nursing receive | Baseline critical-care assessment, devices/lines, allergies, risks, and handover from source ward/emergency/theater recorded. | ICU nurse |
| 5 | Intensive monitoring | High-frequency vitals, ICU observations, intake/output, ventilator/device parameters as applicable. | ICU nurse |
| 6 | Critical alerts | Open alerts raised for deterioration; acknowledged and resolved with audit trail. | ICU nurse / Intensivist |
| 7 | ICU doctor review | Intensivist/consultant performs ICU round, updates working diagnosis and care plan. | Doctor / Intensivist |
| 8 | Inpatient orders | Lab, radiology, medication, procedure, consult orders placed on IPD encounter. | Doctor |
| 9 | Service execution | Departments fulfill orders; results return to ICU detail and IPD timeline. | Lab / Radiology / Pharmacy / Nursing |
| 10 | Continuous care loop | Monitor → review → adjust plan → repeat until stable for step-down or discharge planning. | ICU team |
| 11 | Transfer or step-down | Internal ICU bed move, isolation, or step-down to ward with handover. | Bed manager / Doctor / ICU nurse |
| 12 | End ICU stay | `end-icu-stay` closes active stay when patient leaves ICU level of care. | Intensivist / ICU charge nurse |
| 13 | Discharge readiness | ICU signals readiness; IPD/Discharge own clearance workflow. | Doctor / ICU nurse |
| 14 | Ward or exit | Patient continues on IPD ward or proceeds through IPD discharge — encounter stays open until IPD closure. | Ward team / Discharge desk |

This loop prevents ICU from becoming a disconnected silo and supports real hospital escalation and step-down patterns per [ipd-flow §8–§9](./ipd-flow.mdc).

---

## 4. ICU Entry Paths

### 4.1 Emergency → ICU

1. Patient stabilized in emergency.
2. Emergency clinician sets ICU disposition.
3. IPD admission created (may use `Billing Deferred` per [ipd-flow §2.1](./ipd-flow.mdc)).
4. ICU bed allocated with priority.
5. `start-icu-stay` opens ICU stay.
6. Patient appears on **Active ICU** board with emergency case context.

### 4.2 OPD → IPD → ICU

1. OPD doctor dispositions to `ADMITTED` ([opd-flow §3, §7](./opd-flow.mdc)).
2. IPD encounter created and linked to source OPD encounter.
3. Admission desk / bed manager assigns ICU bed.
4. `start-icu-stay` when patient is received in ICU.
5. ICU detail shows read-only OPD source context (visit type, disposition note, consulting doctor).

**Rule:** OPD `ADMITTED` completes the outpatient visit; ICU must not duplicate OPD or IPD admission records.

### 4.3 Ward escalation to ICU

1. Ward doctor or nurse requests ICU transfer ([ipd-flow §9](./ipd-flow.mdc)).
2. Transfer approved and completed to ICU bed (`update-transfer` with `to_bed_id`).
3. `start-icu-stay` if not already active.
4. Handover note captured on transfer.

### 4.4 Theater post-op → ICU

1. Theater completes procedure with ICU recovery disposition.
2. Patient transferred to ICU bed.
3. ICU workspace shows theatre case summary when API provides reference.
4. `start-icu-stay` and post-op monitoring begin.

### 4.5 Planned ICU admission

1. Elective admission scheduled to ICU/NICU ([ipd-flow §2.3](./ipd-flow.mdc)).
2. Pre-auth/deposit completed per policy before routine admission.
3. Bed reserved; patient admitted; ICU stay opened on arrival.

