## 5. Backend Queue and Filter Contract

Frontend labels, filters, summary cards, badges, dialogs, and actions must use backend ICU filters on `GET /ipd-flows` as canonical workflow states. Prefer IPD-flow ICU actions over standalone `/icu-stays` CRUD for clinical workspace mutations.

| Backend filter / scope | User meaning | Primary owner |
| ---------------------- | ------------ | ------------- |
| `icu_queue_scope=ACTIVE` + `icu_status=ACTIVE` | Patient has active ICU stay | ICU nurse / Intensivist |
| `has_critical_alert=true` | Open critical alert needs action | ICU nurse / Intensivist |
| `transfer_status=REQUESTED` (or equivalent) | Step-down or ICU transfer pending | Bed manager / ICU charge |
| `stage=DISCHARGE_PLANNED` + active ICU stay | Discharge readiness in progress | Doctor / ICU nurse |
| `icu_status=ENDED` | Recent step-down / historical ICU stay | ICU supervisor / Audit |
| `icu_queue_scope=WITH_ICU` | All admissions with any ICU history | Supervisor / Reporting |
| `include_icu=true` | Detail/list includes ICU overlay DTO | All ICU roles |

Default landing scope: **Active ICU**.

---

## 6. ICU Stay Lifecycle

| Status | Meaning |
| ------ | ------- |
| `No active stay` | Patient on ICU board eligible but stay not opened |
| `ACTIVE` | ICU stay in progress; patient `In ICU` per [ipd-flow §11](./ipd-flow.mdc) |
| `ENDED` | Step-down completed; patient may be `In Ward` on same IPD encounter |

### Lifecycle actions

| Action | API | When valid |
| ------ | --- | ---------- |
| Start ICU stay | `POST /ipd-flows/:id/start-icu-stay` | Eligible admission, no active stay, ICU bed assigned or escalation complete |
| End ICU stay | `POST /ipd-flows/:id/end-icu-stay` | Active stay; step-down or pre-discharge from ICU level of care |

**Rules:**

- Prevent duplicate active stays (`icu_stay_already_active` → user-friendly message).
- Ending ICU stay does **not** close the IPD encounter.
- After step-down, patient remains on IPD ward board.

---

## 7. ICU Bed Management

ICU module owns an **ICU-ward scoped bed board**; hospital-wide bed CRUD remains in Facility settings / IPD bed board ([ipd-flow §14.2](./ipd-flow.mdc)).

| Item | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| ICU ward filter | Medical ICU, surgical ICU, NICU, isolation ICU units |
| Bed status | Available, reserved, occupied, cleaning, maintenance, blocked |
| Bed assignment | Via IPD `assign-bed` with ICU bed picker |
| Transfer complete | Via IPD `update-transfer` with `to_bed_id` |
| Suitability | Enforce isolation/equipment/payer blocking reasons from API |

Link **View in IPD** for hospital-wide bed operations.

---

## 8. Monitoring, Observations, Vitals, and Critical Alerts

| Task | API / pattern | Owner |
| ---- | ------------- | ----- |
| ICU observation | `POST …/add-icu-observation` | ICU nurse |
| Vitals | Encounter-scoped vital signs CRUD | ICU nurse |
| Critical alert | `POST …/add-critical-alert` | ICU nurse / Any authorized clinician |
| Resolve alert | `POST …/resolve-critical-alert` | Intensivist / ICU nurse |

- Open alerts drive shell nav badge and **Critical alerts** queue.
- Observation and alert events sync to IPD timeline (`ICU_OBSERVATION` events).
- Nursing module may show shared vitals/MAR; ICU owns stay-scoped observations and alerts.

---

## 9. ICU Rounds and Clinical Assessment

During ICU care, the intensivist should be able to:

1. Review admission source, allergies, active orders, pending results, open alerts, devices.
2. Record ICU round note (extend `add-ward-round` with structured fields when API supports them).
3. Update working diagnosis, plan, lines/devices, goals of care.
4. Decide continue ICU care, step-down, or discharge readiness.

---

## 10. Inpatient Orders from ICU

All orders attach to the IPD encounter and route to department queues ([ipd-flow §7](./ipd-flow.mdc)).

| Order type | Shared UI | Billing |
| ---------- | --------- | ------- |
| Lab | `clinical_lab_order_action_dialog.dart` | `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel` |
| Radiology | `clinical_radiology_order_action_dialog.dart` | `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel` |
| Medication | `clinical_prescription_action_dialog.dart` | `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel` |
| Procedure / consult / nursing instructions | Per catalog/API availability | Per policy gates |

Charges post to IPD bill automatically; ICU does not run cashier workflows.

---

## 11. Transfers and Step-Down

| Transfer type | ICU module behavior |
| ------------- | ------------------- |
| Step-down to ward | Request → approve → complete with target bed; prompt **end ICU stay** |
| ICU bed transfer | Same ward type; may keep active stay |
| Isolation | Transfer with infection-control reason |
| Theater | Temporary movement for procedure |
| External | Referral out; IPD handles encounter outcome |

Full lifecycle: `request-transfer` → `update-transfer` (approve, start, complete, cancel). Require `to_bed_id` on complete.

---

## 12. Discharge Readiness and Clearance Handoff

ICU signals readiness; IPD/Discharge/Billing own clearance ([ipd-flow §10–§12](./ipd-flow.mdc)).

| ICU action | API | Outside ICU |
| ---------- | --- | ----------- |
| Mark discharge readiness | `plan-discharge` | Pharmacy, billing, nursing clearance |
| Show substates | Read from API when available | IPD discharge panel, Billing workspace |

**Rule:** Do not show “patient discharged” until IPD `DISCHARGED` stage.

---

## 13. Billing and Insurance (read-mostly in ICU UI)

Per [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc):

- Show `Billing Deferred`, deposit status, pre-auth, running balance when API provides.
- Emergency path: proceed-first-bill-later when policy allows.
- Elective high-cost procedures: gate on clearance when required.
- Link to Billing workspace for deposits and interim bills.

---

## 14. Key ICU Actions by Role

| Role | Allowed actions |
| ---- | --------------- |
| ICU nurse | Vitals, observations, critical alerts, MAR visibility, handover, transfer support |
| Intensivist / Doctor | ICU rounds, orders, discharge readiness, transfer approval |
| ICU charge nurse / Bed manager | ICU bed board, assign bed, transfer complete, start/end stay coordination |
| Billing | Clearance links only — no ICU clinical mutations |
| `icuManager` | Full ICU workspace per entitlement model |

Actions visible only when backend state and role both allow them.

