## 15. Recommended ICU Module Design

Two primary views, clearly separated:

### 15.1 ICU Patient Board (default)

| Column | Purpose |
| ------ | ------- |
| Patient | Name, display ID, age/sex |
| Admission No. | IPD encounter number |
| ICU stay status | Active, ended, none |
| Ward / Bed | Current ICU location |
| Consultant | When API provides |
| ICU start / LOS | Time in critical care |
| Acuity / alert severity | Critical alert chip |
| Transfer state | Pending step-down |
| Next action | Hospital-language next step |

Summary cards filter the board ([opd-flow §6](./opd-flow.mdc) pattern). Hide zero-value cards where workspace pattern expects it.

### 15.2 ICU Bed Board

| Column | Purpose |
| ------ | ------- |
| Ward | ICU unit |
| Room / Bed | Physical location |
| Bed class | ICU, NICU, etc. |
| Bed status | Occupied, available, cleaning, etc. |
| Current patient | If occupied |
| Alert indicator | Open critical alert |
| Next action | Assign, transfer, clean |

---

## 16. Status-Based Available Actions

| Current state | Available actions |
| ------------- | ----------------- |
| Eligible, no active stay | Start ICU stay, assign ICU bed, request transfer to ICU |
| Active ICU stay | Record vitals/observation, raise/resolve alerts, ICU round, orders, request transfer, discharge readiness |
| Critical alert open | Resolve alert, record observation, notify intensivist |
| Transfer pending | Approve, complete (with bed), cancel |
| Discharge planned | Mark readiness updates, link to IPD/Billing clearance, end ICU stay if still active |
| ICU stay ended | View history, open IPD workspace; ward care continues |

Action panel hierarchy: unstable monitoring → resolve alerts → clinical orders → transfer step-down → discharge readiness → end ICU stay (destructive last).

