## 18. Module Boundaries

From [app-write-up.mdc](../app-write-up.mdc):

| Own in ICU | Do not duplicate — use other module |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------- |
| ICU stays, monitoring, critical alerts, ICU rounds | IPD admission creation, ward rounds for non-ICU patients |
| ICU-ward bed board view | Hospital-wide bed CRUD (Facility / IPD) |
| Discharge **readiness** signal | Full discharge clearance (Discharge / IPD / Billing) |
| ICU-scoped observations and alerts | Ward nursing care plans and MAR (Nursing) |
| Order placement with billing choice | Invoice/payment/cashier (Billing) |
| Bedside equipment display (if API links) | Equipment maintenance (Biomedical) |

---

## 19. Important Implementation Rule

The **IPD encounter remains the central record** ([ipd-flow §16](./ipd-flow.mdc)). ICU overlay data attaches to it:

- ICU stay start/end
- ICU observations and vitals
- Critical alerts
- ICU round notes
- Orders and results (via IPD encounter)
- Transfer history
- Discharge readiness signal
- Source OPD/emergency/theater context (read-only links)

Do **not** duplicate IPD admission lifecycle in ICU. Prefer `ipd-flow` ICU actions as canonical over standalone `/icu-stays` for workspace mutations unless admin/reporting requires direct CRUD.

